# PlatoLives v5.6

## What's New

- **Commodore 64 (VIC-II) Display Engine**: Brings the warmth and tactile nostalgia of the world's most beloved 8-bit home computer to PLATO. Sit in front of a virtual Commodore 1702 CRT monitor or experience the vintage softness of an authentic RF composite connection.
- **Authentic C64 Color Schemes & Phosphors**: Choose between the iconic Two-Tone Classic Blue, full 16-color VIC-II graphics, or calibrated vintage P40 Amber and P31 Green monochrome monitor palettes.
- **Authentic 12.5% Border Frame**: Features the unmistakable C64 outer border with seamless optical touch compensation, plus a full-screen toggle for maximum workspace.
- **Clean Crisp Hires Option**: Enjoy high-contrast readability of PLATO lessons and notes while preserving authentic 8-bit character charm.
- **Global Input System & Keymapper Refactoring**: Complete priority given to native PLATO keys across Windows, macOS, and Linux, eliminating OS shortcut conflicts (Ctrl+C, Alt mnemonics) and streamlining custom key remapping.
- **Unified Multiplatform Release**: Native performance and parity across macOS (Metal/Cocoa), Windows (Direct3D 11, x86_64 & ARM64), Linux Desktop (OpenGL/SDL2), and Linux Headless Console.
